<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herod the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 73–4 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herod the Great was an Idumaean named king of Judea by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate">Roman Senate</a> in 40 BCE, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the last Hasmonean king in 37 BCE. A Roman client, he rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Temple in Jerusalem</a> and built Caesarea Maritima and fortresses such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masada">Masada</a>. After his death his kingdom was divided among his sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herod-the-great.jpg" alt="Herod the Great" width="320" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HerodtheGreat2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
